          >
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
              <h3 class="h4 text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-dark">Year-by-Year PPF Growth</h3>
              <span class="text-sm text-text-default opacity-70 font-semibold">Compounding Schedule</span>
            </div>

            <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-100 dark:border-[#262938]">
              <table class="w-full text-left text-base sm:text-lg">
                <thead
                  class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-[#1c202e] font-bold text-text-default border-b border-gray-100 dark:border-[#262938]"
                >
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-5 py-4">Year</th>
                    <th class="px-5 py-4">Amount Deposited</th>
                    <th class="px-5 py-4">Interest Earned</th>
                    <th class="px-5 py-4 text-right">Year-End Balance</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody
                  id="ppf-schedule-body"
                  class="divide-y divide-gray-100 dark:divide-[#262938] text-dark font-medium"
                >
                  {/* Filled by the script below. */}
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- How it works & example -->
        <div
          class="bg-white dark:bg-[#14161f] border border-gray-200 dark:border-[#262938] rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 md:p-10 space-y-6"
        >
          <h2 class="h3 font-bold text-dark tracking-tight">How Does a PPF Calculator Work?</h2>
          <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-text-default opacity-85 leading-relaxed font-normal">
            Each year, your new deposit is added to the balance and the whole balance earns interest at the PPF rate.
            That interest is added to the account at the end of the financial year, so next year it earns interest too.
            Over 15 years this compounding does most of the work - which is why depositing early in the year, by 5
            April, earns you the most.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-primary/5 dark:bg-primary/10 border border-primary/20 rounded-2xl p-6 space-y-4">
            <h3 class="h4 text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-primary">Practical Example:</h3>
            <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-text-default font-medium leading-relaxed">
              Suppose you deposit the maximum <strong>₹1,50,000 every year</strong> for <strong>15 years</strong> at an interest
              rate of <strong>7.1% p.a.</strong>:
            </p>
            <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-5 text-sm sm:text-base pt-2">
              <li
                class="bg-white dark:bg-[#1c202e] border border-gray-200 dark:border-[#262938] rounded-xl p-4 space-y-1"
              >
                <span class="block text-text-default opacity-70 font-semibold text-xs sm:text-sm"
                  >Total Investment:</span
                >
                <span class="font-extrabold text-dark text-lg sm:text-xl">₹22,50,000</span>
              </li>
              <li
                class="bg-white dark:bg-[#1c202e] border border-gray-200 dark:border-[#262938] rounded-xl p-4 space-y-1"
              >
                <span class="block text-text-default opacity-70 font-semibold text-xs sm:text-sm"
                  >Tax-Free Interest Earned:</span
                >
                <span class="font-extrabold text-primary text-lg sm:text-xl">₹18,18,209</span>
              </li>
              <li
                class="bg-white dark:bg-[#1c202e] border border-gray-200 dark:border-[#262938] rounded-xl p-4 space-y-1"
              >
                <span class="block text-text-default opacity-70 font-semibold text-xs sm:text-sm">Maturity Value:</span>
                <span class="font-black text-dark text-xl sm:text-2xl">₹40,68,209</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Formula -->
        <div
          class="bg-white dark:bg-[#14161f] border border-gray-200 dark:border-[#262938] rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 md:p-10 space-y-6"
        >
          <h2 class="h3 font-bold text-dark tracking-tight">What is the PPF Calculator Formula?</h2>
          <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-text-default opacity-85 leading-relaxed font-normal">
            With a fixed deposit made at the start of every year and yearly compounding, the maturity value is:
          </p>

          <div
            class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-[#181b25] border border-gray-200 dark:border-[#262938] rounded-2xl p-6 text-center font-mono text-lg sm:text-2xl font-black text-primary overflow-x-auto"
          >
            Maturity (F) = P × [ ( (1 + i)^n - 1 ) / i ] × (1 + i)
          </div>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-5 text-sm sm:text-base">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-[#1c202e] border border-gray-100 dark:border-[#262938] rounded-xl p-4">
              <strong class="text-primary block text-base sm:text-lg font-bold mb-1">F (Maturity Value)</strong>
              <span class="opacity-80">The balance in your PPF account at the end of the period.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-[#1c202e] border border-gray-100 dark:border-[#262938] rounded-xl p-4">
              <strong class="text-primary block text-base sm:text-lg font-bold mb-1">P (Yearly Deposit)</strong>
              <span class="opacity-80">The amount you deposit each financial year (₹500 to ₹1,50,000).</span>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-[#1c202e] border border-gray-100 dark:border-[#262938] rounded-xl p-4">
              <strong class="text-primary block text-base sm:text-lg font-bold mb-1">i (Interest Rate)</strong>
              <span class="opacity-80">Annual PPF interest rate / 100.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-[#1c202e] border border-gray-100 dark:border-[#262938] rounded-xl p-4">
              <strong class="text-primary block text-base sm:text-lg font-bold mb-1">n (Number of Years)</strong>
              <span class="opacity-80">How many years you deposit and hold the account (15 or more).</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Tax-saving options comparison -->
